talia","francia","espana-regreso"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Small, green, and big-hearted. Travels with her backpack, explorer hat, and lenses to discover the unseen.","es":"Pequeña, verde y de corazón inmenso. Viaja con su mochila, sombrero de exploradora y lentes para ver lo invisible."},"slug":"curileta","species":"Lagartija Curiosa del Bosque Encantado","values":["Curiosidad por el mundo","Amistad incondicional","Amor por el hogar"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“True adventure is not just imagining places, but feeling them beneath your paws!”","es":"«¡El verdadero viaje no consiste solo en imaginar lugares, sino en sentirlos bajo tus patitas!»"},"name":"Curileta"}'::jsonb, 5, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'emi', 'emi', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Clay amulet of the Nile","es":"Amuleto de arcilla del Nilo"}],"biography":{"en":"Emi guides Curileta through the secret corridors of the Great Pyramid.","es":"Emi guía a Curileta a través de los pasadizos de la Gran Pirámide, mostrándole los jeroglíficos ancestrales y recordándole el valor de la constancia."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Can roll spheres 50 times his own body weight.","es":"Capaz de rodar esferas que superan 50 veces su propio peso."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":86,"courage":94,"curiosity":90,"wisdom":99},"gallery":[],"id":"emi","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Emi the beetle of Egypt","es":"Emi el escarabajo de Egipto"},"url":"/images/characters/emi-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Guardian of the Secret Passages of Giza","es":"Guardián de los Pasadizos Secretos de Guiza"},"personality":["Filosófico","Tenaz","Amable","Perspicaz"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["egipto"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Wise dung beetle. Teaches Curileta that in the desert, the greatest treasure is shade.","es":"Escarabajo pelotero sabio y trabajador. Enseña a Curileta que en el desierto el mayor tesoro es la sombra."},"slug":"emi","species":"Escarabajo Pelotero Sagrado de Egipto","values":["Trabajo duro","Humildad"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Seeking treasure? In this blazing desert, true treasure is shade.”","es":"«¿Buscas el tesoro? En este desierto ardiente, el verdadero tesoro es la sombra.»"},"name":"Emi el Escarabajo"}'::jsonb, 6, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'emu', 'emu', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Dark emerald green emu eggshell","es":"Cáscara vacía de huevo verde esmeralda oscuro"}],"biography":{"en":"Curileta dodges playful pecks as the emu examines her hat. Later at Hyams Beach, she spots a dark emerald emu egg.","es":"Curileta debe esquivar ágilmente sus picotazos cuando el emú se interesa por el llamativo color de su sombrero. Más tarde, en Hyams Beach, descubre un impresionante huevo de emú de color verde esmeralda oscuro."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Can sprint at over 50 km/h across the desert with powerful legs.","es":"Sus patas son tan potentes que puede correr a más de 50 km/h por el desierto."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":97,"courage":86,"curiosity":98,"wisdom":78},"gallery":[],"id":"emu","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Curious emu on Australian plains","es":"Emú curioso en la llanura australiana"},"url":"/images/characters/emu-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Swift Outback Runner & Hat Inspector","es":"Veloz Corredor del Outback & Catador de Sombreros"},"personality":["Curioso","Acelerado","Simpático","Incansable"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["australia"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Giant flightless Australian bird. Curiously tries to peck Curileta’s explorer hat.","es":"Pájaro gigante no volador de Australia. Intenta picotear con curiosidad el sombrero de aventurera de Curileta."},"slug":"emu","species":"Emú Australiano","values":["Persistencia","Espíritu aventurero"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“What a fascinating hat! Can it be eaten or is it for collecting stars?”","es":"«¡Qué sombrero tan fascinante! ¿Se come o es para coleccionar estrellas?»"},"name":"El Emú Curioso"}'::jsonb, 7, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'gino', 'gino', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Tiny white chef hat","es":"Gorro minúsculo de chef blanco"},{"en":"Spatula for pistachio gelato","es":"Espátula para servir gelato de pistacho"}],"biography":{"en":"From Rome to Venice canals, Gino shares Italy’s culinary art with Curileta.","es":"Desde los museos de Roma hasta las góndolas de Venecia y la Torre inclinada de Pisa, Gino acompaña a Curileta a saborear más de 350 tipos de pasta y el auténtico gelato artesanal."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Helped Curileta use her tail as a paintbrush in Florence.","es":"Ayudó a Curileta a usar su colita como pincel para pintar en una plaza de Florencia."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":97,"courage":84,"curiosity":93,"wisdom":89},"gallery":[],"id":"gino","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Gino the mouse chef in Italy","es":"Gino el ratoncito chef en Italia"},"url":"/images/characters/gino-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Master Pizzaiolo & Gelato Connoisseur","es":"Maestro Pizzaiolo & Catador de Gelato"},"personality":["Apasionado","Expresivo","Gourmet","Creativo"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["italia"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Florentine mouse chef who shows Curileta that cuisine and fine art go hand in hand.","es":"Ratoncito florentino con gorro de chef que enseña a Curileta que la comida y el arte van de la mano."},"slug":"gino","species":"Ratón de Campo Italiano","values":["Amor por el arte","El sabor de compartir"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Mamma mia! In Italy pizza dough flies like a saucer and gelato tastes like heaven!”","es":"«¡Mamma mia! ¡En Italia la masa de pizza vuela como platillo y el gelato sabe a gloria!»"},"name":"Gino el Ratoncito Chef"}'::jsonb, 8, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'joey', 'joey', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Reinforced thread stitching and ultra-soft cotton","es":"Costuras de hilo reforzado y relleno de algodón ultra suave"}],"biography":{"en":"Joey is a soft plush koala with fluffy ears. Dropped in the Outback during kangaroo leaps, Curileta rescued him intact to reunite him with baby kangaroo.","es":"Joey es un muñeco de trapo suave con forma de koala y orejas esponjosas. Se cayó accidentalmente en el Outback mientras la familia canguro saltaba cerca de Uluru. Curileta lo rescató intacto entre la tierra roja, devolviendo la sonrisa al bebé canguro."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"In the original book, Joey is explicitly the baby kangaroo’s plush koala toy.","es":"En el libro original, Joey es el peluche de koala del bebé canguro y no el nombre del bebé."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":60,"courage":80,"curiosity":70,"wisdom":90},"gallery":[],"id":"joey","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Joey the plush koala","es":"Joey el koala de trapo"},"url":"/images/characters/joey-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"The World’s Most Traveled Plush Toy","es":"El Peluche Más Viajero del Mundo"},"personality":["Silencioso","Reconfortante","Suave","Incondicional"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["australia"],"shortDescription":{"en":"The baby kangaroo’s inseparable plush koala. His loss sparks Curileta’s thrilling search at Uluru.","es":"El inseparable koala de peluche del bebé canguro. Su extravío desata la gran búsqueda de Curileta en Uluru."},"slug":"joey","species":"Peluche de Koala de Trapo","values":["Consuelo","Amor a la infancia","Ternura"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“(A gentle and fluffy hug that calms any storm)”","es":"«(Un abrazo suave y esponjoso que calma cualquier tempestad)»"},"name":"Joey (El Koala de Trapo)"}'::jsonb, 9, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'kiki', 'kiki', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Reflective silver fern leaf","es":"Hoja de helecho plateado reflectante"}],"biography":{"en":"Kiki reveals glowworm caves, Maori Haka dance, and Hobbiton burrows to Curileta.","es":"Kiki muestra a Curileta las cuevas de gusanitos de luz bioluminiscente, los poblados maoríes con la danza de la Haka y las diminutas casitas de Hobbiton."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Has no wings but nostrils at the tip of his beak scent food underground.","es":"No tiene alas pero su olfato en la punta del pico es más fino que el de un sabueso."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":88,"courage":82,"curiosity":94,"wisdom":95},"gallery":[],"id":"kiki","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Kiki the Kiwi among ferns","es":"Kiki el Kiwi en los bosques de helechos"},"url":"/images/characters/kiki-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Night Guide of Waitomo Caves","es":"Guía Nocturno de las Cuevas de Waitomo"},"personality":["Tímido","Amable","Nocturno","Divertido"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["nueva-zelanda"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Round, flightless bird who guides Curileta beneath subterranean constellations.","es":"Pájaro redondo y sin alas que guía a Curileta bajo las constelaciones subterráneas de Nueva Zelanda."},"slug":"kiki","species":"Pájaro Kiwi de Nueva Zelanda","values":["Preservación de la magia","Orgullo de la propia tierra"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Kia ora! Look up at the cave ceiling: down here, stars shine underground!”","es":"«¡Kia ora! ¡Mira hacia el techo de la cueva: aquí las estrellas brillan bajo la tierra!»"},"name":"Kiki el Kiwi"}'::jsonb, 10, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'lola', 'lola', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Orange blossom sprig with sweet aroma","es":"Ramita de azahar de Sevilla con aroma dulce"},{"en":"Pouch of golden saffron for paella","es":"Sobre con azafrán dorado para la paella"}],"biography":{"en":"Amid orange blossoms and flamenco rhythm, Lola reveals that home is found with the heart.","es":"Entre el olor al azahar de Sevilla y el taconeo del flamenco, Lola entrega a Curileta la clave secreta: el Bosque Encantado no se encuentra con los pies, sino orientando el mapa del corazón."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"The invisible forest portal is marked by a stone matching her silhouette.","es":"La entrada invisible al bosque está custodiada por una roca que tiene exactamente su misma silueta."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":70,"courage":95,"curiosity":89,"wisdom":100},"gallery":[],"id":"lola","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Lola the tortoise in Spain","es":"Lola la tortuga mora en España"},"url":"/images/characters/lola-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Guardian of the Invisible Portal","es":"La Guardiana de la Entrada Invisible"},"personality":["Serena","Sabia","Cálida","Agradecida"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["espana-regreso"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Wise Andalusian tortoise who guides Curileta’s heart back to the Enchanted Forest.","es":"Sabia tortuga andaluza que guía el corazón de Curileta de vuelta al Bosque Encantado en España."},"slug":"lola","species":"Tortuga Mora de España","values":["Raíces culturales","El verdadero significado del hogar"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“The forest you seek is not found with feet, but with the heart.”","es":"«El bosque que buscas no se encuentra con los pies, sino con el corazón.»"},"name":"Lola la Tortuga Mora"}'::jsonb, 11, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'lulu', 'lulu', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Ball of pure warm llama wool","es":"Ovillo de lana virgen de vicuña y llama"},{"en":"Sample of multicolored Andean potatoes","es":"Muestrario de patatas multicolores andinas"}],"biography":{"en":"Lulú welcomes Curileta onto her back across the stone paths of the Inca citadel.","es":"Lulú recibe a Curileta en los senderos de piedra de la ciudad inca. Le presta su lana caliente para protegerla del frío y la lleva en su lomo para contemplar la arquitectura antisísmica de los Andes."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Her fleece was so warm it protected Curileta all through Iceland.","es":"Su lana es tan térmica que protegió a Curileta durante todo su viaje por los glaciares de Islandia."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":82,"courage":88,"curiosity":85,"wisdom":92},"gallery":[],"id":"lulu","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Lulú the llama at Machu Picchu","es":"Lulú la llama andina en Machu Picchu"},"url":"/images/characters/lulu-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Andean Guardian of the Cloud Peaks","es":"Protectora Andina de las Cumbres"},"personality":["Generosa","Tranquila","Acogedora","Fuerte"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["peru"],"shortDescription":{"en":"A warm-fleeced giant llama who shelters Curileta from the chill of Machu Picchu.","es":"Una llama gigante y de lana tibia que cobija a Curileta del aire frío de Machu Picchu."},"slug":"lulu","species":"Llama Lanuda de los Andes","values":["Hospitalidad","Calor de hogar"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Climb onto my back, little lizard: on freezing peaks, warmth is meant to be shared.”","es":"«Sube a mi lomo, pequeña lagartija: en las cumbres frías, el calor se comparte.»"},"name":"Lulú la Llama"}'::jsonb, 12, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'ornitorrinco', 'ornitorrinco', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Polished pebble from clear creek bed","es":"Piedrecita pulida del fondo del arroyo cristalino"}],"biography":{"en":"With duck bill, beaver tail, and webbed feet, platypus delights Curileta as one of nature’s most fascinating marvels.","es":"Con su pico de pato, cola de castor y patas palmeadas, el ornitorrinco sorprende a Curileta por ser uno de los seres más insólitos y fascinantes del reino animal, demostrando que la naturaleza adora la originalidad."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Detects prey movements in water using electromagnetic sensors in its bill.","es":"Detecta los movimientos de presas en el agua mediante impulsos electromagnéticos en su pico."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":92,"courage":82,"curiosity":90,"wisdom":96},"gallery":[],"id":"ornitorrinco","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Platypus swimming in the creek","es":"Ornitorrinco nadando en el arroyo"},"url":"/images/characters/ornitorrinco-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Guardian of the Secret Creeks","es":"Guardián de los Riachuelos Secretos"},"personality":["Tranquilo","Enigmático","Observador","Pacífico"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["australia"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Unique dweller of the Australian creek. Curileta almost steps on him while searching for the plush in the Outback.","es":"Habitante único del riachuelo australiano. Curileta casi lo pisa mientras busca el peluche en el Outback."},"slug":"ornitorrinco","species":"Ornitorrinco Australiano","values":["Autenticidad","Armonía fluvial"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Being uniquely different is the greatest gift nature can bestow.”","es":"«Ser diferente es el mejor regalo que la naturaleza nos puede conceder.»"},"name":"El Ornitorrinco Sabio"}'::jsonb, 13, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'pez-volador', 'pez-volador', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Miniature drops of phosphorescent sea water","es":"Gotas de agua marina fosforescente en miniatura"}],"biography":{"en":"During Curileta’s Pacific voyage, Glub glides across glowing waves, sharing the marvels of nocturnal marine life.","es":"Durante la travesía marina de Curileta por el Pacífico occidental, Glub y sus compañeros despliegan sus aletas translúcidas planeando sobre el agua iluminada por plancton fosforescente, maravillando a la pequeña exploradora."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Can glide over 200 meters above water surface using its pectoral fins.","es":"Puede planear más de 200 metros sobre la superficie del agua desplegando sus aletas pectorales."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":99,"courage":91,"curiosity":94,"wisdom":84},"gallery":[],"id":"pez-volador","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Glub the flying fish gliding over water","es":"Glub el pez volador planeando sobre el mar"},"url":"/images/characters/pez-volador-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Wave Acrobat & Bioluminescent Navigator","es":"Acróbata de las Olas & Navegante Bioluminiscente"},"personality":["Acróbata","Divertido","Luminoso","Vivaz"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["mar-filipinas"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Flying fish of the Philippine Sea. Leaps alongside the ship deck revealing night ocean secrets.","es":"Pez volador del Mar de Filipinas. Salta junto a la cubierta del barco y revela los secretos del océano nocturno."},"slug":"pez-volador","species":"Pez Volador del Pacífico","values":["Libertad marina","Curiosidad sin fronteras"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“The sea does not end at the surface: sometimes we take flight to touch reflected stars!”","es":"«¡El mar no termina en la superficie: a veces volamos para tocar las estrellas reflejadas!»"},"name":"Glub el Pez Volador"}'::jsonb, 14, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'picu', 'picu', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Volcanic bread baked underground","es":"Trozo de pan volcánico horneado bajo tierra"}],"biography":{"en":"Picu admires Curileta’s courage and shows her the volcanic heat beneath polar snow.","es":"Picu admira la valentía de Curileta al viajar desde tierras cálidas. Le enseña cómo la Tierra guarda calor volcánico bajo la nieve y cómo hornear pan bajo tierra."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Dives over 60 meters in icy waves to catch fish.","es":"Bucea a más de 60 metros bajo las olas heladas para pescar arenques."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":96,"courage":89,"curiosity":92,"wisdom":84},"gallery":[],"id":"picu","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Picu the puffin in Iceland","es":"Picu el frailecillo en Islandia"},"url":"/images/characters/picu-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Guardian of Ice and Geysers","es":"Guardián del Hielo y los Géiseres"},"personality":["Divertido","Valiente","Expresivo","Acróbata"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["islandia"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Colorful-billed puffin. Swims with Curileta in the geothermal lagoons of Iceland.","es":"Pájaro de pico multicolor con aspecto de payaso simpático. Nada con Curileta en las aguas termales de Islandia."},"slug":"picu","species":"Frailecillo Ártico de Islandia","values":["Alegría ante la adversidad","Convivencia con la naturaleza"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“It takes true bravery to travel this far! Snow falls above while warm waters embrace us below.”","es":"«¡Es de valientes viajar tan lejos! La nieve cae arriba pero el agua tibia nos abraza abajo.»"},"name":"Picu el Frailecillo"}'::jsonb, 15, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'pompon', 'pompon', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Carved wooden mailbox for travel letters","es":"Buzón de madera tallada para las cartas de viaje"},{"en":"Postage stamp album from all continents","es":"Álbum con sellos postales de todos los países"},{"en":"Golden feather sent from New Zealand","es":"Pluma dorada enviada desde Nueva Zelanda"}],"biography":{"en":"Pompón is Curileta’s best friend who stays in the Enchanted Forest keeping their roots safe while receiving letters from every continent.","es":"Pompón es el mejor amigo de Curileta. Permanece en el Bosque Encantado custodiando las raíces del hogar mientras Curileta recorre el mundo. Aunque no viaja físicamente con ella, su amor y fidelidad lo mantienen conectado a Curileta a través de cada carta, cada sello y cada regalo que ella le envía."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"When overjoyed, leaps so high he almost touches the highest branches.","es":"Cuando se pone muy feliz salta tan alto que casi toca las ramas del árbol más alto."},{"en":"Curileta discovered that in Peru he has Andean cousins called Cuyes.","es":"Curileta descubrió que en Perú tiene parientes andinos llamados Cuyes (conejillos de indias)."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":95,"courage":75,"curiosity":80,"wisdom":88},"gallery":[],"id":"pompon","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Pompón the bunny under the tree","es":"Pompón el conejito bajo el árbol"},"url":"/images/characters/pompon-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Faithful Forest Guardian & Keeper of Letters","es":"El Fiel Guardián del Hogar & Destinatario de Cartas"},"personality":["Tierno","Fiel","Hogareño","Alegre","Saltarín"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["espana-inicio","espana-regreso"],"shortDescription":{"en":"White rabbit with a tender heart. Stays in the Enchanted Forest guarding the home and receiving Curileta’s letters under the tallest tree.","es":"Conejito blanco de corazón tierno. Permanece en el Bosque Encantado custodiando el hogar y esperando cada carta de Curileta bajo el árbol más alto. No viaja físicamente por el mundo."},"slug":"pompon","species":"Conejito Blanco del Bosque Encantado","values":["Amistad sincera","Paciencia","Cuidado de las raíces"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Whenever a letter arrives, I feel the whole world fits right into our tree!”","es":"«¡Siempre que llega una carta tuya, siento que el mundo entero cabe en nuestro árbol!»"},"name":"Pompón"}'::jsonb, 16, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'quetzal', 'quetzal', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Iridescent emerald feather of fortune","es":"Pluma esmeralda iridiscente de la fortuna"},{"en":"Ancestral cacao bean","es":"Semilla de cacao ancestral (el chocolate de los dioses)"}],"biography":{"en":"Atop the Sun Pyramid, Quetzal reveals how ancient pyramids spoke with the stars.","es":"En la cima de la Pirámide del Sol, Quetzal revela a Curileta que las pirámides son un gigantesco calendario de piedra para comunicarse con el universo y que el eco en Kukulcán imita su propio canto."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Claps at Chichen Itza pyramid reproduce his precise bird call.","es":"El eco de las palmadas en la pirámide de Chichén Itzá reproduce exactamente su canto."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":100,"courage":92,"curiosity":95,"wisdom":98},"gallery":[],"id":"quetzal","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Quetzal in flight","es":"Quetzal en vuelo majestuoso"},"url":"/images/characters/quetzal-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Star Guardian of Mesoamerica","es":"Guardián de las Estrellas de Mesoamérica"},"personality":["Místico","Majestuoso","Sabio","Ágil"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["mexico"],"shortDescription":{"en":"Sacred bird with emerald feathers. Teaches Curileta the dance of the planets atop Teotihuacan.","es":"Ave sagrada de plumas verdes esmeralda. Enseña a Curileta el baile de los planetas en Teotihuacán."},"slug":"quetzal","species":"Ave Sagrada Quetzal","values":["Conexión cósmica","Respeto al pasado"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Stones are not merely rocks: they are calendars to converse with the stars.”","es":"«Las piedras no son solo rocas: son calendarios para hablar con las estrellas.»"},"name":"Quetzal"}'::jsonb, 17, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('character', 'zipi-bot', 'zipi-bot', '{"backpackItems":[{"en":"Mini solar battery and melody speaker","es":"Batería solar miniatura y altavoz con canciones"}],"biography":{"en":"Amid futuristic Tokyo, Zipi-Bot shows Curileta how technology and ancient temples thrive together.","es":"En medio del bullicio futurista de Tokio y las vías del tren bala Shinkansen, Zipi-Bot enseña a Curileta que la tecnología y las tradiciones milenarias pueden convivir en perfecta armonía."},"curiosityFacts":[{"en":"Can sing Japanese melodies while cleaning floors.","es":"Sabe cantar melodías japonesas mientras ayuda a limpiar el suelo."}],"explorerStats":{"agility":85,"courage":80,"curiosity":97,"wisdom":94},"gallery":[],"id":"zipi-bot","mainImage":{"alt":{"en":"Zipi-Bot the robot in Tokyo","es":"Zipi-Bot el robot en Tokio"},"url":"/images/characters/zipi-bot-main.webp"},"passportRole":{"en":"Singing Robot of Tokyo","es":"Pequeño Robot Cantor de Tokio"},"personality":["Entusiasta","Musical","Curioso","Leal"],"relatedBooks":["las-aventuras-de-curileta"],"relatedEpisodes":[],"relatedLocations":["japon"],"shortDescription":{"en":"A lovable lost toy robot that Curileta helps reunite with his owner in Japan.","es":"Un entrañable robot de juguete perdido que Curileta ayuda a reencontrarse con su dueño en Japón."},"slug":"zipi-bot","species":"Robot Interactivo de Juguete","values":["Solidaridad","Armonía entre tradición y futuro"],"voiceQuote":{"en":"“Beep-boop! In Tokyo the future and ancient temples ride the same bullet train!”","es":"«¡Bip-bop! ¡En Tokio el futuro y los templos milenarios viajan en el mismo tren bala!»"},"name":"Zipi-Bot"}'::jsonb, 18, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('collaboration', 'publishing', null, '{"category":"publishing","desc":{"en":"International publishing rights, co-editions, and translations in global markets.","es":"Derechos internacionales de publicación, coedición y traducción en nuevos mercados."},"iconName":"Building2","id":"publishing","orderIndex":1,"title":{"en":"Publishing & Distribution","es":"Editoriales & Distribución"}}'::jsonb, 1, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('collaboration', 'licensing', null, '{"category":"licensing","desc":{"en":"Official lines of toys, stationery, fashion, and immersive brand experiences.","es":"Líneas oficiales de juguetes, papelería, moda y experiencias inmersivas de marca."},"iconName":"Award","id":"licensing","orderIndex":2,"title":{"en":"Licensing & Merchandising","es":"Licensing & Merchandising"}}'::jsonb, 2, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('collaboration', 'media', null, '{"category":"press","desc":{"en":"Official press kit, high-resolution media assets, and interview bookings.","es":"Dossier de prensa oficial, kit de imagen de alta resolución y entrevistas."},"iconName":"Newspaper","id":"media","orderIndex":3,"title":{"en":"Media, Press & Festivals","es":"Medios, Prensa & Festivales"}}'::jsonb, 3, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'mexico', null, '{"body":{"en":["Mexico is incredible! I tasted something called “chocolate,” invented here long ago, but back then it was spicy!","I climbed a pyramid so tall I nearly touched the clouds. Also, we lizards have dragon-like relatives here called Iguanas.","Plus, at Chichén Itzá, clapping in front of Kukulcán pyramid echoes exactly like the sacred Quetzal song!","And in Puebla lies the Cuexcomate volcano: only 13 meters tall, I climbed it in a flash!"],"es":["¡México es increíble! He probado algo llamado “chocolate”, que aquí inventaron hace mucho tiempo, ¡pero el de antes era picante!","He subido a una pirámide tan alta que casi toco las nubes. Por cierto, aquí las lagartijas tenemos parientes que parecen dragones y se llaman Iguanas.","Además, he aprendido cosas asombrosas: en Chichén Itzá, si aplaudes frente a la pirámide de Kukulcán, ¡el eco suena exactamente como el canto del Quetzal!","Y en Puebla está el volcán Cuexcomate: ¡mide solo 13 metros y lo escalé en un segundo!"]},"city":{"en":"Teotihuacan & CDMX","es":"Teotihuacán & CDMX"},"country":{"en":"Mexico","es":"México"},"envelopeColor":"from-amber-950/90 to-yellow-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Dear Pompón:","es":"Querido Pompón:"},"id":"mexico","order":1,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Mayans and Aztecs chewed tree resin, giving birth to modern chewing gum!","es":"Los mayas y aztecas obtenían la resina para mascarla. ¡Así nació el chicle que conocemos!"},"tag":"ORIGEN DEL CHICLE","title":{"en":"Chicozapote Tree Resin","es":"Resina de Chicozapote"}},{"fact":{"en":"The “food of the gods” served as sacred currency among ancient Aztecs.","es":"El “alimento de los dioses” (Theobroma cacao) funcionaba como moneda de intercambio."},"tag":"MONEDA ANCESTRAL","title":{"en":"mmm... Spicy Chocolate","es":"mmm... Chocolate Picante"}},{"fact":{"en":"World’s tiniest volcano, right in the city with a spiral staircase to its crater.","es":"El volcán más diminuto del planeta, en medio de la ciudad con una escalera de caracol."},"tag":"VOLCÁN ENANO","title":{"en":"Cuexcomate Volcano (13m)","es":"Volcán Cuexcomate (13m)"}}],"postageColor":"#f59e0b","postmark":"TEOTIHUACÁN • 19.69°N • CARTA 01","signOff":{"en":"P.S. Sending you photos I took for you. Miss you! With love, Curileta.","es":"P.D. Te envío algunas fotos que me he tomado para ti. ¡Te echo de menos! Con amor, Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 1, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'peru', null, '{"body":{"en":["I reached a sanctuary so high clouds drift past your knees. It’s Machu Picchu! I made a woolly friend named Lulú the Llama.","Mountains have faces and stones tell stories! Did you know there are over 3,000 potato varieties here?","Inca masonry is so precise not even a card fits through. In earthquakes, the stones dance and settle right back!","And I found your fluffy relatives! Cuyes (guinea pigs) are celebrated throughout the Andes."],"es":["He llegado a un lugar tan alto que las nubes te pasan por las rodillas. Se llama Machu Picchu. He hecho una nueva amiga muy peluda que me ha prestado su lana para no tener frío: ¡la llama Lulú!","¡Aquí las montañas tienen caras y las piedras cuentan historias! He descubierto que existen más de 3.000 tipos de patatas diferentes. ¡Imagínate una cena con tantas opciones!","Las piedras incas encajan con tanta precisión que no cabe ni una tarjeta. Y cuando hay terremotos, ¡bailan y vuelven a su lugar exacto!","Por cierto, ¡he visto a tus parientes! Los Cuyes (conejillos de indias) son famosísimos aquí en los Andes."]},"city":{"en":"Machu Picchu & Cusco","es":"Machu Picchu & Cusco"},"country":{"en":"Peru","es":"Perú"},"envelopeColor":"from-emerald-950/90 to-teal-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Hello again, Pompón!","es":"¡Hola de nuevo, Pompón!"},"id":"peru","order":2,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Purple, yellow, striped, and golden spuds grown across vertical mountain terraces.","es":"Moradas, amarillas, rayadas y doradas cultivadas en terrazas agrícolas verticales."},"tag":"BIODIVERSIDAD","title":{"en":"3,000 Potato Varieties","es":"3.000 Tipos de Patatas"}},{"fact":{"en":"Giant animal geoglyphs preserved for millennia in the rainless desert sand.","es":"Dibujos gigantes de animales en el desierto conservados por la falta de viento."},"tag":"MISTERIO ANDINO","title":{"en":"Mysterious Nazca Lines","es":"Líneas de Nazca"}},{"fact":{"en":"Native to the Andes, revered and painted across centuries of folklore.","es":"No vienen de la India, sino de los Andes. ¡Aparecen en cuadros y leyendas antiguas!"},"tag":"PARIENTES DE POMPÓN","title":{"en":"Andean Guinea Pigs (Cuy)","es":"Conejillos de Indias (Cuy)"}}],"postageColor":"#10b981","postmark":"MACHU PICCHU • 2.430m • CARTA 02","signOff":{"en":"A bouncy leap of love, Curileta.","es":"Un abrazo saltarín, Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 2, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'egipto', null, '{"body":{"en":["You won’t believe what happened! Crossing the ocean, a monster tempest struck. With my sticky paws I climbed the mast and secured the helm!","Now writing from Egypt, where the sun shines like molten gold. The Great Pyramid has over 2 million stone blocks heavier than elephants!","Emi the Dung Beetle taught me that the true treasure of the sands is shade, guiding me through hieroglyphic corridors.","And ancient Egyptians slept on wooden or stone headrests to preserve elaborate hairstyles!"],"es":["¡No vas a creer lo que me pasó! Cruzando el océano en el viejo galeón, una tormenta gigante sacudió el barco. Con mis patitas pegajosas trepé al mástil y amarré una cuerda suelta. ¡Salvé el timón y el viaje!","Ahora te escribo desde Egipto, donde el sol brilla como oro fundido. Estoy frente a la Gran Pirámide: ¡hecha con más de 2 millones de bloques que pesan más que un elefante!","He conocido a un Escarabajo Pelotero llamado “Emi”. Me enseñó que el verdadero tesoro del desierto es la sombra, y me guió por pasadizos secretos llenos de jeroglíficos.","¿Y sabes qué? ¡Los antiguos egipcios dormían con almohadas de madera o piedra para no estropear sus peinados!"]},"city":{"en":"Giza & Nile River","es":"Guiza & Río Nilo"},"country":{"en":"Egypt","es":"Egipto"},"envelopeColor":"from-amber-950/90 to-orange-950/80","greeting":{"en":"My dearest Pompón!","es":"¡Mi querido Pompón!"},"id":"egipto","order":3,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Flows south to north, giving life and black silt to bloom in the desert.","es":"Fluye de sur a norte regando todo el desierto. ¡Sin su limo negro no habría flores!"},"tag":"AGUA SAGRADA","title":{"en":"The South-to-North Nile","es":"Río Nilo que Fluye al Revés"}},{"fact":{"en":"Carved to circulate cool air around the neck beneath blazing 80°C heat.","es":"Talladas para dejar circular el aire fresco por el cuello bajo el sol de 80°C."},"tag":"INVENTO EGIPCIO","title":{"en":"Stone Headrest Pillows","es":"Almohadas de Piedra"}},{"fact":{"en":"Symbol of the rising sun Ra, rolling his sphere with tireless patience.","es":"Símbolo del sol naciente Ra, empujando su esfera de vida con infinita paciencia."},"tag":"GUÍA DEL DESIERTO","title":{"en":"Emi the Dung Beetle","es":"Escarabajo Pelotero Emi"}}],"postageColor":"#eab308","postmark":"GIZA • VALLE DEL NILO • CARTA 03","signOff":{"en":"Miss you dearly, Pompón! Sand kisses, Curileta.","es":"¡Te extraño mucho, Pompón! Muchos besitos de arena, Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 3, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'islandia', null, '{"body":{"en":["Brrr! Writing with one paw while warming the other. Iceland is like a volcano and an ice cube becoming best friends!","Suddenly BOOM! A geyser shot boiling water into the clouds. Picu the Puffin showed me the warm Blue Lagoon as snowflakes fell.","At night, green and purple lights dance across the sky: Northern Lights! They even bake bread underground with volcano heat for 24h.","And there isn’t a single mosquito on the entire island! Fewer snacks for a lizard, but wonderful for exploring!"],"es":["¡Brrr! Te escribo esta carta con una patita mientras me caliento la otra. ¡He llegado a Islandia! Es como si un volcán y un cubito de hielo se hubieran hecho mejores amigos.","Caminando por lava negra, ¡BOOM! Un géiser disparó agua hirviendo hacia el cielo. Menos mal que conocí a Picu el Frailecillo, que me invitó a un baño caliente en la Laguna Azul mientras caían copos de nieve.","Por la noche, el cielo se llena de luces verdes y moradas que bailan solas: ¡las Auroras Boreales! Y aquí hornean el pan enterrándolo bajo la tierra cerca de las zonas volcánicas.","¿Lo mejor? ¡No hay ni un solo mosquito en toda la isla! Aunque para mí hay menos snacks, ¡para explorar es genial!"]},"city":{"en":"Blue Lagoon & Geysers","es":"Laguna Azul & Géiseres"},"country":{"en":"Iceland","es":"Islandia"},"envelopeColor":"from-sky-950/90 to-blue-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Dear Pompón!","es":"¡Querido Pompón!"},"id":"islandia","order":4,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Sweet rye bread baked slowly for 24 hours in boiling geothermal ground.","es":"Masa horneada durante 24 horas con el calor natural de manantiales hirvientes."},"tag":"MAGIA VOLCÁNICA","title":{"en":"Underground Volcano Bread","es":"Pan Volcánico Bajo Tierra"}},{"fact":{"en":"Solar wind colliding with Earth’s atmosphere in glowing emerald curtains.","es":"Partículas solares chocando contra la atmósfera terrestre en cortinas de seda verde."},"tag":"CIELO MÁGICO","title":{"en":"Dancing Auroras","es":"Auroras Boreales Danzantes"}},{"fact":{"en":"Natural subterranean pressure pots erupting 20-meter steaming geysers.","es":"Ollas a presión naturales que disparan chorros de agua pura a más de 20 metros."},"tag":"FUERZA PURA","title":{"en":"Geysers of the Earth","es":"Géiseres con Hipo"}}],"postageColor":"#38bdf8","postmark":"REYKJAVÍK • 64.96°N • CARTA 04","signOff":{"en":"A tight warm hug against the frost. Your brave explorer, Curileta.","es":"Te mando un abrazo muy apretado para no perder el calor. Tu exploradora valiente, Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 4, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'japon', null, '{"body":{"en":["Kon’nichiwa! Japan is thrilling! I rode the Shinkansen bullet train which flies so fast my reflection lagged behind.","I helped Zipi-Bot, a lost toy robot, reunite with his owner. He even sings cheerful melodies!","I saw cube-shaped watermelons, special bathroom-only slippers, and cafes dedicated to petting friendly owls and cats.","And I gazed upon Mount Fuji: a sacred volcano so symmetrical it looks hand-drawn, topped with a crisp snowy hat."],"es":["¡Kon’nichiwa! ¡Japón es el lugar más loco y divertido que he visitado! Me subí al Shinkansen (tren bala) que vuela tan rápido que mi reflejo en el cristal se quedó atrás.","Allí conocí a Zipi-Bot, un pequeño robot de juguete perdido al que ayudé a encontrar a su dueño. ¡Incluso canta canciones alegres!","He visto sandías con forma de cubo para que quepan en la nevera, zapatillas exclusivas para entrar al baño, y cafeterías donde la gente va solo para acariciar búhos y gatos.","Y he contemplado el Monte Fuji: un volcán sagrado tan perfecto que parece dibujado con un lápiz y coronado con un sombrero blanco de nieve."]},"city":{"en":"Tokyo & Mount Fuji","es":"Tokio & Monte Fuji"},"country":{"en":"Japan","es":"Japón"},"envelopeColor":"from-rose-950/90 to-red-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Hello, my dear Pompón!","es":"¡Hola, mi querido Pompón!"},"id":"japon","order":5,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Grown inside glass molds so they don’t roll away in compact refrigerators.","es":"Cultivadas dentro de cajas de cristal para que no rueden y encajen en las baldas."},"tag":"INVENTO CURIOSO","title":{"en":"Square Watermelons","es":"Sandías Cuadradas"}},{"fact":{"en":"Three volcanoes layered in one, revered as the spiritual symbol of sunrise.","es":"Son en realidad tres volcanes superpuestos, venerados como símbolo del amanecer."},"tag":"VOLCÁN SAGRADO","title":{"en":"Sacred Mount Fuji","es":"Monte Fuji Sagrado"}},{"fact":{"en":"Ultra-modern robots live side by side with peaceful ancient wooden shrines.","es":"En Japón la tecnología convive en perfecta armonía con los templos milenarios."},"tag":"FUTURO Y TRADICIÓN","title":{"en":"Zipi-Bot & Companions","es":"Zipi-Bot & Robots"}}],"postageColor":"#f43f5e","postmark":"TOKIO • SHINKANSEN • CARTA 05","signOff":{"en":"Sayonara, from your friend Curileta.","es":"Sayonara, de tu amiga Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 5, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'australia', null, '{"body":{"en":["Everything is upside-down here! I rescued baby kangaroo Joey’s toy koala in the vast red Outback.","In thanks, Mama Kangaroo gave me a ride in her pouch with 4-meter leaps! I felt what it’s like to fly without wings.","I met the platypus: duck bill, beaver tail, otter feet, and lays eggs! Nature’s most charming puzzle.","At Hyams Beach, I walked upon the whitest sand on Earth: so pure it squeaks like sugar beneath your paws."],"es":["¡Aquí todo está al revés! He rescatado el peluche de un bebé canguro llamado Joey en pleno desierto rojo del Outback.","En agradecimiento, ¡Mamá Canguro me llevó en su marsupio y dimos saltos de 4 metros en el aire! Sentí lo que es volar sin tener alas.","He conocido al ornitorrinco: ¡tiene pico de pato, cola de castor, patas de nutria y pone huevos! Es el chiste más divertido de la naturaleza.","Y en Hyams Beach caminé sobre la arena más blanca del planeta: es tan pura que chirría como azúcar bajo las patitas."]},"city":{"en":"Uluru & Hyams Beach","es":"Uluru & Hyams Beach"},"country":{"en":"Australia","es":"Australia"},"envelopeColor":"from-orange-950/90 to-amber-950/80","greeting":{"en":"My dearest Pompón! G’day mate!","es":"¡Mi queridísimo Pompón! G’day mate!"},"id":"australia","order":6,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Egg-laying mammal that senses electrical impulses underwater with its bill.","es":"Mamífero que detecta la electricidad de otros seres acuáticos bajo el agua."},"tag":"PUZZLE VIVIENTE","title":{"en":"The Curious Platypus","es":"Ornitorrinco Confuso"}},{"fact":{"en":"Shifts shades from sunrise amber to fiery sunset crimson across the desert.","es":"Cambia de color del naranja amanecer al rojo escarlata ardiente en el ocaso."},"tag":"CORAZÓN ROJO","title":{"en":"Uluru Sacred Rock","es":"Roca Roja de Uluru"}},{"fact":{"en":"Weighs as much as 12 hen eggs, looking like carved emerald stone for ground camouflage.","es":"Pesa como 12 huevos de gallina y parece una esmeralda tallada para camuflaje."},"tag":"COLOR MÁGICO","title":{"en":"Dark Green Emu Egg","es":"Huevo de Emú Verde Oscuro"}}],"postageColor":"#ea580c","postmark":"OUTBACK • ULURU • CARTA 06","signOff":{"en":"A giant kangaroo leap of love, Curileta.","es":"Un salto gigante de amor, tu amiga Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 6, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:13Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'nueva-zelanda', null, '{"body":{"en":["New Zealand feels like a fairy tale! Silver fern forests gleam in the moonlight.","Kiki the Kiwi showed me Waitomo cave: underground ceilings dotted with thousands of blue glowworms sparkling like sapphire galaxies.","Then I discovered Hobbiton: velvet hills with tiny round-door houses smelling of blackberry pie. Perfectly sized for me!","I even practiced the Maori Haka, stamping my lizard feet with strength."],"es":["¡He llegado a Nueva Zelanda y me sentí en un cuento de hadas! Los bosques de helechos plateados brillan bajo la luz de la luna.","Kiki el Kiwi me llevó a la cueva de Waitomo: bajo tierra, el techo estaba cubierto por miles de gusanitos luminosos que brillaban como constelaciones de zafiro.","Luego descubrí Hobbiton: colinas de terciopelo con casitas diminutas de puertas redondas y chimeneas que huelen a pastel de moras. ¡Eran perfectas para mi tamaño!","Y aprendí a bailar la Haka maorí sacando la lengua y golpeando el suelo con mis patitas."]},"city":{"en":"Waitomo & Hobbiton","es":"Waitomo & Hobbiton"},"country":{"en":"New Zealand","es":"Nueva Zelanda"},"envelopeColor":"from-emerald-950/90 to-green-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Hello, my dear Pompón!","es":"¡Hola, mi querido Pompón!"},"id":"nueva-zelanda","order":7,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Bioluminescent glowworms turning limestone cave ceilings into starfields.","es":"Gusanitos de luz que iluminan cuevas calizas como un cielo nocturno estrellado."},"tag":"CONSTELACIÓN SUBTERRÁNEA","title":{"en":"Waitomo Glowworm Skies","es":"Cielos Bajo Tierra en Waitomo"}},{"fact":{"en":"Dug right into lush green hills with working hearths and tiny flower gardens.","es":"Construidas dentro de las colinas verdes con huertos y chimeneas activas."},"tag":"REINO DIMINUTO","title":{"en":"Hobbit Round Doors","es":"Casitas con Puertas Redondas"}},{"fact":{"en":"Silver leaf undersides reflect moonlight to guide travelers in deep forests.","es":"El envés de sus hojas refleja la luz lunar y guiaba a los guerreros en la noche."},"tag":"GUÍA NATURAL","title":{"en":"Silver Ferns (Cyathea)","es":"Helechos Plateados"}}],"postageColor":"#059669","postmark":"WAITOMO • HOBBITON • CARTA 07","signOff":{"en":"With warm hugs and a “Kia ora”, your friend Curileta.","es":"Con mucho cariño y un “Kia ora” (¡hola!), tu amiga Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 7, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'china', null, '{"body":{"en":["I am strolling atop the spine of a stone dragon! The Great Wall spans over 21,000 kilometers across mountain ridges.","In a bamboo grove I met panda Bao. He chomps up to 12 kg of bamboo daily! He carried me on his head to watch the sunset from the highest tower.","Writing here uses meaningful characters instead of letters. Bao taught me to paint the symbol for Friendship!","And fireworks were invented here to scatter bad spirits and light up festivals with color."],"es":["¡Estoy caminando sobre la espalda de un dragón de piedra! La Gran Muralla tiene más de 21.000 kilómetros subiendo y bajando montañas.","En un bosquecillo de bambú conocí al panda Bao. ¡Come hasta 12 kilos de bambú al día! Me llevó sobre su cabeza hasta la torre más alta para contemplar la puesta de sol.","Aquí no escriben con letras como las nuestras, sino con caracteres mágicos. ¡Bao me enseñó a dibujar el que significa Amistad!","Y descubrí que aquí se inventaron los fuegos artificiales para espantar a los malos espíritus y llenar la noche de estrellas de colores."]},"city":{"en":"Great Wall & Beijing","es":"Gran Muralla & Pekín"},"country":{"en":"China","es":"China"},"envelopeColor":"from-red-950/90 to-rose-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Ni Hao, my dear Pompón!","es":"¡Ni Hao, mi querido Pompón!"},"id":"china","order":8,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Stretches across deserts and peaks, appearing from above like a resting dragon.","es":"La Gran Muralla recorre desiertos, valles y cumbres como un dragón guardián."},"tag":"MURALLA INFINITA","title":{"en":"The Stone Dragon","es":"El Dragón de Piedra"}},{"fact":{"en":"Signifies two hands clasped together walking the explorer’s road.","es":"Representa dos manos unidas ayudándose en el camino del explorador."},"tag":"TRAZOS SAGRADOS","title":{"en":"Character of Friendship","es":"Carácter de la Amistad (友)"}},{"fact":{"en":"Tapping two fingers gently on the table says “thank you” without breaking tea silence.","es":"Golpear dos dedos suavemente en la mesa es el código de gratitud silenciosa."},"tag":"ARTE DEL TÉ","title":{"en":"Sharing Tea with Bao","es":"Bebiendo Té con Bao"}}],"postageColor":"#dc2626","postmark":"GRAN MURALLA • 21.000km • CARTA 08","signOff":{"en":"With lots of love and a warm panda hug, Curileta.","es":"Con mucho amor y un abrazo de oso panda, tu amiga Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 8, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'italia', null, '{"body":{"en":["I arrived in the boot-shaped country! The aroma of basil and warm crust fills every cobblestone street.","In Florence I met mouse chef Gino, who showed me over 350 pasta shapes!","I tasted pistachio gelato: as green as my lizard skin, perfect camouflage and silky smooth!","I posed holding up the Leaning Tower of Pisa with my paws: tilted 4 meters for centuries on soft soil!"],"es":["¡He llegado al país con forma de bota! La comida aquí huele tan deliciosa que mi nariz no para de moverse.","En Florencia conocí al ratoncito chef Gino. ¡Me enseñó que existen más de 350 formas de pasta diferentes!","He probado el Gelato artesanal: el de pistacho era tan verde como yo y me sirvió de camuflaje. ¡Es mucho más cremoso que el helado común!","Y me tomé una foto intentando sujetar la Torre de Pisa con mis patitas: lleva cientos de años inclinada 4 metros sobre suelo blando sin caerse."]},"city":{"en":"Florence, Pisa & Venice","es":"Florencia, Pisa & Venecia"},"country":{"en":"Italy","es":"Italia"},"envelopeColor":"from-green-950/90 to-emerald-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Ciao, my dear Pompón!","es":"¡Ciao, mi querido Pompón!"},"id":"italia","order":9,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Served with a flat paddle and denser texture for velvet richness.","es":"Servido con espátula plana y con menos aire para que su sabor sea seda pura."},"tag":"EL MEJOR HELADO","title":{"en":"Pistachio Gelato","es":"Gelato de Pistacho"}},{"fact":{"en":"Tilted on sandy silt; secured by modern engineers so it never falls.","es":"Inclinada por arcilla arenosa; la ingeniería moderna la aseguró para siempre."},"tag":"EQUILIBRIO MÁGICO","title":{"en":"Leaning Tower of Pisa","es":"Torre Inclinada de Pisa"}},{"fact":{"en":"No cars, only singing gondoliers atop thousands of petrified wooden piles in water.","es":"Una ciudad sin coches construida sobre miles de troncos de madera en el agua."},"tag":"CIUDAD SOBRE AGUA","title":{"en":"Venice Floating City","es":"Canales de Venecia"}}],"postageColor":"#16a34a","postmark":"FLORENCIA • PISA • CARTA 09","signOff":{"en":"With lots of “amore” and pizza smiles, Curileta.","es":"Con mucho “amore” y sabor a pizza, tu amiga Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 9, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'francia', null, '{"body":{"en":["I nearly reached France as a sandwich! I hid inside a hollow baguette to escape a dog, and a girl gifted me a strawberry thinking I was a good-luck lizard!","In Paris I climbed the Eiffel Tower. When summer warms the iron, thermal expansion makes it grow several centimeters taller!","At the first tier I tasted a fresh croissant: flaky like autumn leaves and curved like a golden crescent moon.","At the Louvre I played peekaboo with the Mona Lisa: no matter where I scurry, her mysterious eyes follow me!"],"es":["¡Casi llego a Francia convertida en sándwich! Me escondí dentro de una baguette para huir de un perrito curioso en los Alpes, ¡y la niña de la familia me regaló una fresa creyendo que era una lagartija de la suerte!","En París escalé la Torre Eiffel por sus vigas de hierro. Cuando hace calor, el metal se expande y ¡la torre crece varios centímetros!","Allí arriba probé mi primer croissant: crujiente como hojas secas y dorado como una luna creciente. ¡Sabe a nubes y alegría!","En el Museo del Louvre jugué al escondite con la Mona Lisa: no importa a qué lado me mueva con mis patitas, ¡sus ojos siempre me siguen!"]},"city":{"en":"Paris & Versailles","es":"París & Versalles"},"country":{"en":"France","es":"Francia"},"envelopeColor":"from-blue-950/90 to-indigo-950/80","greeting":{"en":"Bonjour, my dear Pompón!","es":"¡Bonjour, mi querido Pompón!"},"id":"francia","order":10,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"Thermal expansion of its iron lattice makes the tower stretch taller in heat.","es":"Los estiramientos térmicos de sus vigas de hierro hacen variar su altura en verano."},"tag":"ESTIRAMIENTO MATINAL","title":{"en":"The Growing Iron Lady","es":"La Dama de Hierro Creciente"}},{"fact":{"en":"Laminated golden dough with butter that crackles crisply with each bite.","es":"Capas de masa hojaldrada con mantequilla que crujen al morder."},"tag":"SABOR A NUBES","title":{"en":"Golden Crescent Croissant","es":"Croissant Luna Creciente"}},{"fact":{"en":"357 mirrors reflecting gardens and chandeliers in a hall of pure gold.","es":"357 espejos que multiplican la luz del sol en un salón de oro."},"tag":"PALACIO REAL","title":{"en":"Hall of Mirrors (Versailles)","es":"Galería de los Espejos (Versalles)"}}],"postageColor":"#2563eb","postmark":"PARÍS • TORRE EIFFEL • CARTA 10","signOff":{"en":"With warm buttery kisses, your friend Curileta.","es":"Con muchos besitos con aroma a mantequilla, tu amiga Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 10, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('letter', 'espana-regreso', null, '{"body":{"en":["I am back! This letter wasn’t mailed: I kept it safe in my pocket to read aloud to you under our tallest tree.","I weathered storms, climbed pyramids, and hugged pandas, but no treasure in the world equals our friendship.","Wise tortoise Lola showed me the Enchanted Forest is found not with paws, but with the heart: invisible to those without curiosity!","I brought golden saffron for an ant paella feast and a backpack brimming with treasures for you."],"es":["¡He vuelto! Esta carta no la envié por correo: la llevé apretada en mi bolsillo para leértela yo misma bajo nuestro árbol.","He cruzado tormentas, escalado pirámides y abrazado pandas, pero ningún tesoro del mundo se compara con tu amistad.","La sabia tortuga Lola me enseñó que el Bosque Encantado no se busca con los pies, sino con el corazón: es invisible para quienes no tienen curiosidad, ¡por eso solo nosotros y nuestros amigos podemos vivir aquí!","He traído un poquito de azafrán dorado para cocinar una paella de hormigas deliciosa y miles de recuerdos en mi mochila para ti."]},"city":{"en":"Enchanted Forest (Home)","es":"Bosque Encantado (Regreso)"},"country":{"en":"Spain","es":"España"},"envelopeColor":"from-amber-950/90 to-emerald-950/80","greeting":{"en":"My dearest Pompón!","es":"¡Mi queridísimo Pompón!"},"id":"espana-regreso","order":11,"photos":[{"fact":{"en":"The tortoise-shaped rock where southern orange blossoms blend with northern pines.","es":"La piedra con forma de tortuga donde el azahar del sur se funde con los pinos del norte."},"tag":"MAPA DEL CORAZÓN","title":{"en":"The Invisible Portal","es":"La Entrada Invisible"}},{"fact":{"en":"Fairy-tale cliffside stone fortresses inspiring legends of adventure.","es":"Fortalezas de cuento de hadas que inspiraron los relatos de caballería."},"tag":"TIERRA DE HISTORIAS","title":{"en":"Castles of Segovia","es":"Castillos de Segovia"}},{"fact":{"en":"The warmest hug after voyaging across five continents of wonders.","es":"El abrazo más cálido tras recorrer los cinco continentes."},"tag":"EL MAYOR TESORO","title":{"en":"Reunion Beneath the Tree","es":"El Reencuentro Bajo el Árbol"}}],"postageColor":"#f59e0b","postmark":"BOSQUE ENCANTADO • CORAZÓN • CARTA 11","signOff":{"en":"And thus I discovered the greatest treasure of all awaits at the end of the road: the place you call “home”. With all my love, Curileta.","es":"Y así comprendí que el mayor tesoro siempre te espera al final del camino: el lugar al que llamas “hogar”. Con todo mi amor, Curileta."}}'::jsonb, 11, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('location', 'australia', 'australia', '{"characters":["curileta","canguro-mama","canguro-bebe","joey","ornitorrinco","emu"],"climate":{"en":"Warm dry Outback desert","es":"Desierto Outback seco y cálido"},"coordinates":{"lat":-25.34,"lng":131.03},"country":{"en":"Australia","es":"Australia"},"curiosities":[{"en":"Hyams Beach holds the Guinness record for whitest sand and squeaks underfoot.","es":"Hyams Beach tiene la arena más blanca del mundo según el récord Guinness y chirría bajo las patitas."},{"en":"Emu eggs are dark green and weigh as much as 12 chicken eggs.","es":"Los huevos de Emú son de color verde oscuro casi negro y pesan como 12 huevos de gallina."},{"en":"The platypus has a duck bill, beaver tail, and is an egg-laying mammal.","es":"El ornitorrinco tiene pico de pato, cola de castor y es mamífero que pone huevos."}],"description":{"en":"The land where Uluru turns from orange to fiery red and sands are the whitest on Earth.","es":"La tierra donde las rocas cambian de naranja a rojo con el sol y la arena de Hyams Beach es la más blanca del mundo."},"heroImage":{"alt":{"en":"Uluru red rock in Australia","es":"Uluru roca roja en Australia"},"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529107386315-e1a2ed48a620?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"},"id":"australia","mentionedPlaces":[],"milestones":[],"name":{"en":"Uluru & Hyams Beach","es":"Uluru & Hyams Beach"},"passportStamp":{"code":"AUS-ULU-06","color":"#EA580C","icon":"Award"},"slug":"australia","theme":{"en":"Red earth, 4-meter leaps with Mama Kangaroo & Joey","es":"Tierra roja, saltos de 4 metros con Mamá Canguro y el peluche Joey"}}'::jsonb, 0, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('location', 'china', 'china', '{"characters":["curileta","bao"],"climate":{"en":"Mountainous continental","es":"Continental montañoso"},"coordinates":{"lat":40.43,"lng":116.57},"country":{"en":"China","es":"China"},"curiosities":[{"en":"The Great Wall measures over 21,000 kilometers in length.","es":"La Gran Muralla mide más de 21.000 kilómetros de longitud."},{"en":"Giant pandas eat up to 12 kilograms of bamboo daily.","es":"Los pandas gigantes como Bao comen hasta 12 kilos de bambú al día."},{"en":"Tapping twice on the table means thank you in silence during tea ceremony.","es":"En la ceremonia del té, dos toques en la mesa significan \"gracias\" en silencio."}],"description":{"en":"An endless wall resembling a stone dragon where panda Bao munches bamboo.","es":"Una muralla infinita que parece la espalda de un dragón de piedra sobre las cumbres, donde el panda Bao come bambú y enseña caracteres mágicos."},"heroImage":{"alt":{"en":"The Great Wall of China at sunset","es":"La Gran Muralla China al atardecer"},"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508804185872-d7badad00f7d?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"},"id":"china","mentionedPlaces":[],"milestones":[],"name":{"en":"The Great Wall & Bamboo","es":"La Gran Muralla & Bambú"},"passportStamp":{"code":"CHN-BEI-08","color":"#DC2626","icon":"Shield"},"slug":"china","theme":{"en":"The 21,000km stone dragon, panda Bao & friendship tea","es":"El dragón de piedra de 21.000 km, el panda Bao y el té de la amistad"}}'::jsonb, 1, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('location', 'egipto', 'egipto', '{"characters":["curileta","emi"],"climate":{"en":"Sunny desert up to 80°C","es":"Desértico soleado hasta 80°C"},"coordinates":{"lat":29.97,"lng":31.13},"country":{"en":"Egypt","es":"Egipto"},"curiosities":[{"en":"The Nile river flows South to North, unlike most rivers.","es":"El río Nilo fluye de sur a norte, al revés de lo que parece normal."},{"en":"Ancient Egyptians slept on stone or wooden headrests to preserve hairstyles.","es":"Los antiguos egipcios usaban almohadas de piedra o madera para no estropear sus peinados."}],"description":{"en":"Two million stone blocks under the desert sun and hieroglyphs telling pharaoh secrets.","es":"Dos millones de bloques de piedra más pesados que elefantes bajo el sol del desierto y jeroglíficos llenos de secretos de faraones."},"heroImage":{"alt":{"en":"Pyramids of Giza in Egypt","es":"Pirámides de Guiza en Egipto"},"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1503177119275-0aa32b3a9368?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"},"id":"egipto","mentionedPlaces":[],"milestones":[],"name":{"en":"Giza Pyramids & The Nile","es":"Pirámides de Guiza & El Nilo"},"passportStamp":{"code":"EGY-CAI-03","color":"#EAB308","icon":"Sun"},"slug":"egipto","theme":{"en":"Golden heat of Ra, Emi the beetle & magic Nile","es":"El calor dorado de Ra, el escarabajo Emi y el Nilo mágico"}}'::jsonb, 2, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('location', 'espana-inicio', 'espana-inicio', '{"characters":["curileta","pompon"],"climate":{"en":"Temperate Mediterranean breeze","es":"Brisa templada mediterránea"},"coordinates":{"lat":40.41,"lng":-3.7},"country":{"en":"Spain (Departure)","es":"España (Partida)"},"curiosities":[{"en":"An invisible place for those who lack curiosity in their hearts.","es":"Es un lugar invisible para los humanos que no tienen curiosidad en el corazón."}],"description":{"en":"Curileta and Pompón’s secret home. A magical forest where the expedition begins.","es":"El hogar secreto de Curileta y Pompón. Un bosque mágico donde los árboles guardan historias y comienza la gran expedición por el mundo."},"heroImage":{"alt":{"en":"The Enchanted Forest in Spain","es":"El Bosque Encantado en España"},"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1448375240586-882707db888b?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"},"id":"espana-inicio","mentionedPlaces":[],"milestones":[],"name":{"en":"The Enchanted Forest","es":"El Bosque Encantado"},"passportStamp":{"code":"ESP-HOME-00","color":"#10B981","icon":"Compass"},"slug":"espana-inicio","theme":{"en":"The tallest tree, the backpack & promise to Pompón","es":"El árbol más alto, la mochila y la promesa a Pompón"}}'::jsonb, 3, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('location', 'espana-regreso', 'espana-regreso', '{"characters":["curileta","pompon","lola"],"climate":{"en":"Scent of rosemary, pines and orange blossom","es":"Aroma a romero, pinos y azahar"},"coordinates":{"lat":40.41,"lng":-3.7},"country":{"en":"Spain (Homecoming)","es":"España (Llegada)"},"curiosities":[{"en":"The greatest treasure at the journey’s end is the place you call home.","es":"El verdadero tesoro al final de cualquier vuelta al mundo es el lugar al que llamas \"hogar\"."},{"en":"Curileta brought golden saffron to cook a delicious paella with Pompón.","es":"Curileta trajo azafrán para cocinar una paella deliciosa con Pompón."}],"description":{"en":"The triumphant homecoming: Curileta crosses the invisible portal to embrace Pompón.","es":"El reencuentro más esperado: Curileta cruza los Pirineos y la entrada invisible para abrazar a Pompón bajo el árbol más alto."},"heroImage":{"alt":{"en":"Tortoise rock in the Enchanted Forest","es":"Roca con forma de tortuga en el Bosque Encantado"},"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1448375240586-882707db888b?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"},"id":"espana-regreso","mentionedPlaces":[],"milestones":[],"name":{"en":"Return to the Enchanted Forest","es":"Regreso al Bosque Encantado"},"passportStamp":{"code":"ESP-HOME-99","color":"#F59E0B","icon":"Heart"},"slug":"espana-regreso","theme":{"en":"Lola the tortoise, the heart map & final hug with Pompón","es":"La tortuga Lola, el mapa del corazón y el abrazo final con Pompón"}}'::jsonb, 4, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('location', 'francia', 'francia', '{"characters":["curileta"],"climate":{"en":"Temperate with lavender & butter aroma","es":"Templado con aroma a mantequilla y lavanda"},"coordinates":{"lat":48.85,"lng":2.35},"country":{"en":"France","es":"Francia"},"curiosities":[{"en":"The Eiffel Tower expands in heat, growing up to 15 cm in summer.","es":"La Torre Eiffel hace \"estiramientos\" en verano: el metal se dilata y crece hasta 15 cm."},{"en":"The Mona Lisa’s gaze seems to follow you from any corner.","es":"La Mona Lisa parece seguirte con la mirada desde cualquier ángulo de la sala."},{"en":"Versailles Hall of Mirrors contains 357 mirrors sparkling like gold.","es":"La Galería de los Espejos de Versalles tiene 357 espejos que reflejan la luz como oro."}],"description":{"en":"The City of Light where the Eiffel Tower expands in summer sun and croissants taste of joy.","es":"La Ciudad de la Luz donde la Torre Eiffel crece centímetros con el calor del sol y los croissants saben a nubes y alegría."},"heroImage":{"alt":{"en":"Eiffel Tower in Paris","es":"Torre Eiffel de París"},"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1502602898657-3e91760cbb34?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"},"id":"francia","mentionedPlaces":[],"milestones":[],"name":{"en":"Paris, Eiffel Tower & Louvre","es":"París, Torre Eiffel & Louvre"},"passportStamp":{"code":"FRA-PAR-10","color":"#2563EB","icon":"Award"},"slug":"francia","theme":{"en":"Cloud-tasting croissant, playful Mona Lisa & stretching tower","es":"Croissant con sabor a nubes, la Mona Lisa juguetona y la torre que estira"}}'::jsonb, 5, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
  ('location', 'islandia', 'islandia', '{"characters":["curileta","picu"],"climate":{"en":"Polar glacial with thermal springs","es":"Polar glacial con aguas termales"},"coordinates":{"lat":64.96,"lng":-19.02},"country":{"en":"Iceland","es":"Islandia"},"curiosities":[{"en":"Bake bread by burying it in hot volcanic soil for 24 hours.","es":"Hornean pan enterrándolo en la tierra caliente durante 24 horas."},{"en":"Virtually no mosquitoes exist across the island due to the arctic climate.","es":"Casi no hay mosquitos en toda la isla debido al clima ártico."},{"en":"Roads are built around rocks to respect invisible elves.","es":"Las carreteras se desvían para no molestar las rocas sagradas de los elfos."}],"description":{"en":"Where snow falls on Curileta’s hat while soaking in thermal water under aurora skies.","es":"Donde la nieve cae sobre el sombrero de Curileta mientras se baña en agua volcánica tibia y contempla las auroras boreales verdes."},"heroImage":{"alt":{"en":"Blue Lagoon and aurora in Iceland","es":"Laguna Azul y aurora en Islandia"},"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504893524553-b855bce32c67?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"},"id":"islandia","mentionedPlaces":[],"milestones":[],"name":{"en":"Blue Lagoon & Geysers","es":"Laguna Azul & Géiseres"},"passportStamp":{"code":"ISL-REK-04","color":"#38BDF8","icon":"Snowflake"},"slug":"islandia","theme":{"en":"Fire and ice, volcanic bread & auroras","es":"Fuego y hielo, pan volcánico y auroras boreales"}}'::jsonb, 6, true, coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now()), coalesce('2026-10-10T11:52:14Z'::timestamptz, now())),
